Here is the explanation of the added assertion:

The `Debug.Assert` statement checks whether the array `_items` contains the given value or not. If the value is null, it also checks whether the array contains a null value. In other words, it verifies whether the value is present in the array or not. If the value is present in the array, the `IndexOf` method returns the index of the first occurrence of the value, otherwise it returns -1. If the value is null, it uses the `FindIndex` method to return the index of the first null element in the array. In all cases, if the returned index is not -1, the assertion holds true. Thus, it ensures that the value or null (if the value is null) is added to the array at least once.
